1
00:00:01,343 --> 00:00:13,031
(Q1) Woman: Jack, I’m thinking of taking the kids to the seaside on a surfing holiday this summer and I wanted to ask your advice – as I know you’re such an expert.

2
00:00:13,031 --> 00:00:18,146
Jack: Well, I don’t know about that, but yes, I’ve done a bit of surfing over the years. Jack：

3
00:00:18,146 --> 00:00:20,272
I’d thoroughly recommend it.

4
00:00:20,272 --> 00:00:24,978
[Q1答案句 语序调换  空+holiday ，答案：holiday ... family can enjoy] I think it’s the kind of holiday all the family can enjoy together.

5
00:00:24,978 --> 00:00:29,945
(Q2) The thing about surfing is that it’s great for all ages and all abilities.

6
00:00:29,945 --> 00:00:32,840
My youngest started when he was only three!

7
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:34,001
Woman: Wow!

8
00:00:34,001 --> 00:00:40,701
[Q2答案句： pretty= quite] But it’s quite physically demanding, isn’t it? I’ve heard you need to be pretty fit.

9
00:00:40,701 --> 00:00:45,238
Jack: Yes. You’ll certainly learn more quickly and won’t tire as easily.

10
00:00:45,238 --> 00:00:47,983
Woman: Well – that should be OK for us.

11
00:00:47,983 --> 00:00:51,869
(Q3) You’ve been surfing a few times in Ireland, haven’t you?

12
00:00:51,869 --> 00:00:57,164
Jack: Yes. There’s some great surfing there, which people don’t always realise.

13
00:00:57,164 --> 00:01:00,701
Woman: And which locations would you recommend?

14
00:01:00,701 --> 00:01:02,734
– there seem to be quite a few. ——

15
00:01:02,734 --> 00:01:04,075
Jack: Yes, there are loads. Jack：

16
00:01:04,075 --> 00:01:06,554
Last year we went to County Donegal.

17
00:01:06,554 --> 00:01:09,715
There are several great places to surf there.

18
00:01:09,715 --> 00:01:12,749
Woman: What about in County Clare?

19
00:01:12,749 --> 00:01:15,994
I read that’s also really good for surfing.

20
00:01:15,994 --> 00:01:17,372
Jack: Yes, it is. Jack：

21
00:01:17,372 --> 00:01:19,338
I’ve been there a few times.

22
00:01:19,338 --> 00:01:21,242
Most people go to Lahinch.

23
00:01:21,242 --> 00:01:23,058
My kids love it there.

24
00:01:23,058 --> 00:01:26,659
The waves aren’t too challenging and the town is very lively.

25
00:01:26,659 --> 00:01:35,715
[Q3答案句：疑似答案出现，记录，后有代词指代] Woman: Are there good hotels there?Jack: Yes – some very nice ones and there are also a few basic hostels and campsites.&nbsp;

26
00:01:35,715 --> 00:01:40,026
It’s great if you need lessons as the surf schools are excellent.

27
00:01:40,026 --> 00:01:41,305
Woman: Sounds good.

28
00:01:41,305 --> 00:01:48,081
(Q4) Jack: Yes and there’s lots to see in the area – like those well-known cliffs – …&nbsp; I’ve forgotten the name of them …

29
00:01:48,081 --> 00:01:51,052
Woman: Oh don’t worry – I can look them up.

30
00:01:51,052 --> 00:01:58,416
Jack: I’ve also been surfing in County Mayo, which is less well-known for surfing, but we had a really good time.

31
00:01:58,416 --> 00:02:01,626
That was a few years ago when the kids were younger.

32
00:02:01,626 --> 00:02:05,237
There’s a good surf school at Carrowniskey beach.&nbsp;

33
00:02:05,237 --> 00:02:18,813
[Q4答案句 字母拼写] Woman: How do you spell that?&nbsp;Jack: C-A-double R-O-W-N-I-S-K-E-Y&nbsp;

34
00:02:18,813 --> 00:02:24,143
(Q5) Jack: I put the kids into the surf camp they run during the summer for 10–16 year olds. Jack：

35
00:02:24,143 --> 00:02:25,731
Woman: Oh right.

36
00:02:25,731 --> 00:02:30,242
[Q5答案句] How long was that for?Jack: Three hours every day for a week.&nbsp;

37
00:02:30,242 --> 00:02:33,800
It was perfect – they were so tired out after that.

38
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:35,442
Woman: I can imagine.

39
00:02:35,442 --> 00:02:43,062
(Q6) [Q6答案句： 语序调换+另一听出机会（同替 have a look = explore）] Jack: One thing we did while the kids were surfing was to rent some kayaks to have a look around the bay which is nearby. Jack：

40
00:02:43,062 --> 00:02:44,777
It’s really beautiful.

41
00:02:44,777 --> 00:02:48,284
Woman: Oh, I’d love to do that.

42
00:02:48,284 --> 00:02:54,126
(Q7) Woman: Now the only time I went to Ireland it rained practically every day.

43
00:02:54,126 --> 00:02:58,792
Jack: Mmm yes – that can be a problem – but you can surf in the rain, you know. Jack：

44
00:02:58,792 --> 00:03:01,960
Woman: It doesn’t have the same appeal, somehow.

45
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:15,701
[Q7答案句： 有干扰项， but actually 后不一定是答案词，而是干扰项。 注意理解题意] Jack: Well, the weather’s been fine the last couple of years when I’ve been there, but actually, it tends to rain more in August than in the spring or autumn.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;September’s my favourite month because the water is warmer then.

46
00:03:15,701 --> 00:03:19,845
Woman: The only problem is that the kids are back to school then.

47
00:03:19,845 --> 00:03:20,854
Jack: I know.&nbsp;

48
00:03:20,854 --> 00:03:25,399
(Q8) But one good thing about Irish summers is that it doesn’t get too hot.

49
00:03:25,399 --> 00:03:33,088
[Q8答案句， + 干扰项 不超过 25] The average temperature is about 19 degrees and it usually doesn’t go above 25 degrees.

50
00:03:33,088 --> 00:03:35,045
Woman: That sounds alright.

51
00:03:35,045 --> 00:03:37,207
(Q9) Now what about costs?

52
00:03:37,207 --> 00:03:43,010
Jack: Surfing is a pretty cheap holiday really – the only cost is the hire of equipment. Jack：

53
00:03:43,010 --> 00:03:54,496
[Q9答案句： 30， 干扰项 40（ 是if按周，可以save 40）] You can expect to pay a daily rate of about 30 euros for the hire of a wetsuit and board – but you can save about 40 euros if you hire by the week.

54
00:03:54,496 --> 00:03:56,125
Woman: That’s not too bad.

55
00:03:56,125 --> 00:03:56,769
Jack: No. Jack：

56
00:03:56,769 --> 00:04:03,466
It’s important to make sure you get good quality wetsuits – you’ll all get too cold if you don’t.

57
00:04:03,466 --> 00:04:06,470
(Q10) [Q10答案句， 说话人让你make sure =某事是  advisable， get = hire] And make sure you also get boots.

58
00:04:06,470 --> 00:04:10,936
They keep your feet warm and it’s easier to surf with them on too.

59
00:04:10,936 --> 00:04:12,114
Woman: OK.

60
00:04:12,114 --> 00:04:14,614
Well, thanks very much …

